{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578828883,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDg1NTc4MTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4017","origin":"github"},"title":"URL scheme for referencing datasets in a RIA store","message":"This is necessary to conveniently support installation from stores like `store.datalad.org`\n\nI think something like this could work:\n\n`ria://\u003clabel or host\u003e#\u003cdataset uuid[@\u003ctag/branch/sha]`\n\nThe store label is used to look for potentially available local configuration on store access. The actual dataset location is generated or looked up based on a combination of store location and dataset uuid. Any version indicator is used to tune the cloned repository.\n\nI think I prefer to use a dedicated url scheme (although I am not set on the \"ria\" name), because the datalad RIs have a different focus, and somewhat different semantics.\n\nSome code to perform such location resolution is available at https://github.com/datalad/git-annex-ria-remote/blob/master/ria_remote/install.py but given that we have store.datalad.org it should rather be functionality provided by datalad-core.","files":null}]}